/* Copyright 2026 Rhett Creighton - Apache License 2.0
 *
 * purpose: The index of verified-fact topics. This file, plus the topic
 *          files it includes, is the whole fact table compiled into z23-dev.
 *
 * WHY THIS EXISTS. Owner directive, 2026-09-05: "always be building things
 * you need to know into z23 so you don't have to burn tokens to learn in the
 * future." Before this table, the same maps of the landing path, the board
 * protocol and the lint system were re-derived from source by each AI reader
 * that needed them, at roughly a hundred thousand tokens a time, several
 * times a day, and the result died with that reader's context. A map that is
 * not in the tree is not knowledge; it is a bill that comes due again.
 *
 * Include with BOTH macros defined; either may be a no-op:
 *
 *   ZCL_FACT_TOPIC(topic, blurb)
 *       topic — dotted topic id, e.g. "landing.proof".
 *       blurb — one short phrase naming what the topic covers.
 *
 *   ZCL_FACT(topic, key, claim, path, anchor)
 *       topic  — the enclosing ZCL_FACT_TOPIC's id, repeated on every row so
 *                a row is meaningful when it is read alone.
 *       key    — snake_case, unique within the topic.
 *       claim  — ONE sentence, at most 160 chars, no tab and no quote. What
 *                is true, in the words the next reader needs.
 *       path   — repo-relative file the claim was read from.
 *       anchor — a literal substring, at most 80 chars, that must still be
 *                findable in that file. The anchor is what makes the row a
 *                FACT rather than an opinion: when the code moves, the
 *                anchor stops matching and the gate fails.
 *
 * A topic is one file. Adding a topic is two lines here plus that file;
 * nothing else in the tree changes, and no reader keeps a second list.
 *
 * tools/lint/check_orient_facts.sh proves every path and every anchor on
 * every commit and has no baseline and no exemption list. NEVER weaken an
 * anchor to make a stale row pass — rewrite the row against what the code
 * now says, or delete it. See docs/zrc/0006-knowledge-in-the-checkout.md.
 *
 * Read by tools/command/native_dev_orient.c and by nothing else; there is no
 * second copy of this table anywhere. */

ZCL_FACT_TOPIC("naming",
               "what the short names in this tree mean: zfc, zfctmp, ZFB1, "
               "zpkgswm, ZRC, and which binary is which")
#include "naming.def"

